It's kind of a long story (which I'll post if I manage to ascend this
character), but my starting pet wound up as a stone golem by the time
I reached the bottom of the Barbarian quest level. Here he met his end
by picking a fight with some kind of troll. So, now there's "a statue
of a stone golem named Satchel" memorializing his valiant stand.
Perhaps this is poignant in its own right, but I'd like to bring him
back, if I can. My starting pets rarely last that long when I play a
hack-and-slash class. Frankly, I think he deserves better for all
that.

If I can find a blessed spellbook of stone to flesh, it's just barely
possible for me to cast it, while naked (95% failure rate at XL23 and
INT9). The problem is, statues of stone golems don't come to life -
they turn into a meatball. It's not even a meatball named Satchel, for
goodness sake.

All I can think of is to polymorph him into a statue of something that
*can* be revived with stone-to-flesh. Ever since 3.3.1 (see C60 on the
3.3.0 Known Bugs list), the game has been keeping track of this so
that revived pet statues are peaceful. However, if you polymorph a
"pet statue", it breaks continuity. The game no longer recognizes it
as a former pet, and the statue also loses its name (all polymorphed
items do this, incidentally). If revived with stone to flesh, it comes
back as a hostile monster.

At this point, I really wouldn't be rescuing my pet so much as making
a new one. As far as the game is concerned, my old pet ceased to
exist, and I may as well have polymorphed him into a bag of hammers. I
also risk destroying the statue entirely, which seems especially cold.
At least as a self-made memorial statue, future generations of the
Duali Tribe can send their sons on right-of-passage pilgrimages to the
statue of Satchel, who figures prominently into their legends of the
defeat of Thoth Amon.

...or something.

I'm hoping there's an option I've overlooked. Any ideas?


